WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.000
- [Devin] Thanks to Skillshare

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.850
for keeping LegalEagle in the air.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.280
Learn to think like a lawyer
for free for two months

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.170
by clicking the link in the description.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.730
Attorney General William Barr

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.280
wrote a four page summary
of the Mueller report.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.777
Here are the nine reasons I
don't think it makes any sense.

00:00:14.777 --> 00:00:18.700
(soaring trumpet music)

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.533
Hey, Legal Eagles.

00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:21.580
Today, we're talking
about the Barr Letter.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.340
This is not the Mueller Report,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.230
as a lot of people have reported.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.300
This is a summary of the Mueller Report

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.670
as conveyed by the Attorney General.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.820
The Barr Letter purports to summarize

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.490
the findings of Special
Counsel Robert Mueller

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.880
and his investigation
into the Trump campaign

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.620
and potential ties to

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.680
Russian interference with our election.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.420
When the Barr Letter came out on Sunday,

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.880
I, like many Americans,
read it cover to cover.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:45.940
But there were a couple things

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.610
that stuck out to me as an attorney

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.210
that just didn't make any sense.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.690
So, here are the nine
things that I don't think

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.520
make any sense in the Barr Letter.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.150
Number one: Why does the
Barr Letter only cover

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.550
two of the three facets
of the Mueller Report?

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.460
You might recall that
Robert Mueller was tasked

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.310
with investigating three things.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.500
A criminal investigation into
potential ties with Russia,

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.490
a criminal investigation into potential

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.290
obstruction of justice by the President,

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.910
and number three, a
counter-intelligence investigation

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:16.720
into Russian interference
with the American election.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.750
But the Barr Letter only deals with

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.660
two of the three facets
of the Mueller Report

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.180
and doesn't actually deal with

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.610
the counter-intelligence portions

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:26.390
of the Mueller Investigation.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.950
Why is that information
missing from Barr's letter?

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.170
Barr could have easily provided a summary

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.750
of the counter-intelligence
portion of the investigation,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.180
but for some reason, he chose not to.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.540
Why is that information not there?

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.700
And we also learned that
Barr is going to make

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.170
a separate summary that can only be given

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.600
to the Gang of Eight instead of the full

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.200
Intelligence Committees in
the House and the Senate.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.850
So, why is there information
that can only be provided

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.040
to the Gang of Eight when a summary,

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.160
even a top-level summary,
can't be provided

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.620
in the letter that is released
to Congress in general

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.780
and to the American people?

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.920
Number two: What does Barr mean

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.647
when he says that the
Mueller Report, quote,

00:02:03.647 --> 00:02:05.790
"did not establish", end quote,

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.700
a conspiracy with the Russians?

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.460
What does it mean to not
establish in this context?

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.770
The Barr Letter quotes a
portion of the Mueller Report

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.797
stating that, quote, "The
investigation did not establish

00:02:16.797 --> 00:02:18.987
"that members of the
Trump Campaign conspired

00:02:18.987 --> 00:02:21.677
"or coordinated with
the Russian government

00:02:21.677 --> 00:02:23.980
"in its election
interference activities.".

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.840
The problem is that this phrase

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.960
can mean wildly different things.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.490
Does it mean that there
was no evidence at all

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.810
or does it mean that there
is a boatload of evidence

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.480
but there is not quite enough to meet

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.380
the standard of beyond a reasonable doubt

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.830
that is necessary for
a criminal prosecution?

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:41.200
If a prosecutor says that an investigation

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.140
did not establish something,

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.680
it doesn't mean that that
thing did not happen.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.010
It doesn't even mean that

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.460
the prosecutor doesn't think it happened.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.900
It means that the investigation

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.220
didn't produce enough information

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.540
to prove beyond a reasonable doubt

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.320
in front of a jury that
that thing happened.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.236
So, in this particular context,

00:02:59.236 --> 00:03:02.130
we don't know which of those
potential outcomes there is.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.160
Is it that there is absolutely no evidence

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.870
or that there is evidence,
but not quite enough

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.190
to meet the legal standard
for a criminal prosecution?

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:12.900
The difference between those
two things is incredibly large

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.130
and is very important as it regards

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.740
what Congress is supposed to do next

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:17.750
with this investigation.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.090
Number three: Why does Barr suggest

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.710
that there can be no
obstruction of justice

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:25.490
when there isn't a conviction
for an underlying crime?

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.360
Attorney General Barr
suggests in his letter

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.260
that you cannot have a conviction
of obstruction of justice

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.730
when there is no underlying criminal act

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.620
or a conviction for an
underlying criminal act,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.180
but that's simply not the case.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.220
A conviction for an
underlying criminal act

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:46.060
is not necessary for a conviction
of obstruction of justice.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.770
Just talk to Martha Stewart, Barry Bonds,

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.360
Bill Clinton, or Kwame Kilpatrick.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.530
The last example is
especially illustrative

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:56.150
because former Detroit
Mayor Kwame Kilpatrick

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.710
went to jail for obstruction of justice

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.320
in 2008 after he lied under oath

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.990
about having an extramarital affair.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.970
Having an affair is not an illegal act

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:09.030
but it's often embarrassing,
especially for politicians,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.360
and they can go to jail
for obstructing justice

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.060
to prevent that information
from coming out.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.630
This is especially
worrying because Barr wrote

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.730
a now famous, perhaps infamous,
19 page memo laying out

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.750
a very idiosyncratic view
of obstruction of justice.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:25.647
In the 19 page memo,
Bar opined that, quote,

00:04:25.647 --> 00:04:27.967
"The President's motive in removing Comey

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:31.417
"and commenting on Flynn
could not have been corrupt

00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:33.187
"unless the President and his campaign

00:04:33.187 --> 00:04:35.830
"were actually guilty
of illegal collusion.".

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.060
The vast majority of legal scholars agree

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.080
that this is simply not the case,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.500
that even in the absence
of an actual guilty verdict

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.320
of illegal collusion or
conspiracy or coordination,

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.470
that is not necessary as a predicate

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.460
for obstructing justice
into that investigation.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.740
But that brings me to point number four:

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.750
Why does Attorney General Barr think

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.340
that there was no crime?

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.280
Even taking Attorney General
Barr's idiosyncratic view

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.720
of obstruction of justice
at face value, even so,

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.710
there was crime that was found
in the Mueller Investigation

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:11.480
and throughout the investigations
into the President.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.740
President Trump is effectively
an unindicted co-conspirator

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:18.440
in a felony campaign finance
violation with Michael Cohen.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.910
Hiding, or at least
preventing, the investigation

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:24.050
into that embarrassing
affair and illegal conduct

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.550
is more than enough
reason to obstruct justice

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.420
and can give rise to
the corrupt mental state

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.610
necessary to be guilty of
obstruction of justice.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:34.740
Potentially, that
investigation was farmed out

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.540
to the Southern District of New York,

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.770
but even still, that is
potential criminal conduct

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.150
that could give rise to
obstruction of justice.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.940
Not to mention all of
the other convictions

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.630
of Papadopoulos, Manafort, and Flynn.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:48.170
So, the question is why would Barr

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:51.870
or Mueller himself
limit the crime at issue

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.530
to the very narrow definition
of Russian conspiracy

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:57.400
that was talked about in the Barr Letter?

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.640
I don't think that makes any sense.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.260
Which takes me to point number five:

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:03.630
Why didn't Robert Mueller
decide the obstruction issue?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.557
The Barr Letter states that, quote,

00:06:05.557 --> 00:06:08.147
"After making a thorough
factual investigation

00:06:08.147 --> 00:06:10.757
"into these matters, the
Special Counsel considered

00:06:10.757 --> 00:06:13.527
"whether to evaluate the conduct
under Department standards

00:06:13.527 --> 00:06:16.167
"governing prosecution
and declination decisions

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:17.827
"but ultimately determined not to make

00:06:17.827 --> 00:06:20.877
"a traditional prosecutorial judgment.

00:06:20.877 --> 00:06:24.957
"The Special Counsel therefore
did not draw a conclusion

00:06:24.957 --> 00:06:26.757
"one way or the other as to whether

00:06:26.757 --> 00:06:29.500
"the examined conduct
constituted obstruction.".

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.310
That doesn't sounds like Robert Mueller

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.240
declined to prosecute because of the facts

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.990
or that there wasn't enough evidence,

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:39.070
but because of some
countervailing legal issue.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.090
Perhaps because of the DOJ policy

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:42.850
not to indict the sitting President.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:44.570
But the Barr Letter goes on to state that,

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.700
instead, for each of the
relevant actions investigated,

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.530
the report sets out evidence
on both sides of the question

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:53.760
and leaves unresolved what
the Special Counsel views

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.530
as difficult decisions of law and fact

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:58.611
concerning whether the
President's actions and intent

00:06:58.611 --> 00:07:00.710
could be viewed as obstruction.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.020
To me, that doesn't make any sense.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.720
If the facts were 50/50, what
we call equipoise in the law,

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.480
that doesn't meet the standard
of beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.540
When there is some evidence but not enough

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:12.130
to reach the very high standard

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.700
of beyond a reasonable doubt,

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.720
then a prosecutor declines to prosecute.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.790
In fact, Mueller
apparently did exactly this

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.700
with the collusion, coordination,

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:25.340
and conspiracy investigation,
which Barr summarizes

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.000
as finding that Mueller did not find

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.460
enough evidence to establish those crimes.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:34.780
So, why did Robert Mueller punt
on the obstruction question

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.850
but not on the collusion
and conspiracy question?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.520
Which brings me to the next
point, point number six:

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.810
Why did William Barr weigh
in on the obstruction issue?

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.120
William Barr is a recent
political appointee

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.840
by President Trump.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.250
The point of the Special Counsel Statute

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:54.800
was for a neutral party to
investigate the executive branch.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.170
If Robert Mueller found enough evidence

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.910
to convict someone for
obstruction of justice,

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.750
the Barr Letter appears to
state that Robert Mueller

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.890
did not decline to prosecute
for obstruction of justice

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.467
because there wasn't enough evidence,

00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:10.400
but because of some other legal issue.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.130
Then does that mean that
Robert Mueller intended

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.940
for William Barr to
weigh in on the question

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.380
or did Robert Mueller intend

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.750
for Congress to answer this question?

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.760
Was it intended to be teed up

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.720
for Congress to make that decision?

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:24.957
Declining to make a, quote,

00:08:24.957 --> 00:08:27.560
"traditional prosecutorial decision"

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:30.850
is not necessarily inviting
the political appointee,

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.740
William Barr, to make that decision.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:35.260
And on top of that, Robert
Mueller, as Special Counsel,

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:38.040
has exclusive jurisdiction in this matter.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.850
Why did he decide not to move forward

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.850
with the obstruction prosecution?

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.580
We know that when Robert Mueller

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.780
does not find enough
evidence to prosecute,

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:48.300
he makes a decision not to prosecute.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.300
But here, in the context
of obstruction of justice,

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.530
Robert Mueller is refusing to
make any decision whatsoever.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.150
We will only know what that means

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:58.410
when the full Mueller Report is revealed.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.570
And on top of that, how is it possible

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.200
that William Barr can make
this decision in 48 hours

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.430
when Robert Mueller couldn't
make the decision in two years?

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:10.730
And was William Barr even able to review

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.860
all of the underlying
evidence in this case?

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.410
We don't even know how long

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.790
the Mueller Report itself actually is.

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.720
Which brings me to point number seven:

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.850
Whose legal conclusions are these

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.840
and are there other legal conclusions

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:23.890
that we haven't seen yet?

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:25.660
The Barr Letter only purports to convey

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.220
Mueller's top-line findings
and does not include

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.610
any of the underlying evidence

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.780
or legal analysis that
undergirds those findings.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.807
The Barr Letter talks about the two, quote

00:09:34.807 --> 00:09:37.400
"principal findings"
of the Mueller Report,

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.150
but does that mean that there are

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.370
other legal findings
that Mueller concluded

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:44.170
that are not part of
these top-line findings?

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:47.190
And as to the legal
conclusions that we have,

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.980
we don't know whether
Attorney General Barr

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.400
concluded that the President

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.410
did not obstruction
justice as a factual matter

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.580
or that it wasn't legally possible

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.500
for him to have obstructed justice.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.840
Again, going back to Barr's
unsolicited 19 page memo,

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.960
he argued a minority position

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.640
that a president effectively
cannot obstruct justice

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.930
when it comes to using
his Article II power.

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.380
And Barr also argued that

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.730
the obstruction of justice statutes

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:14.110
don't apply to the President
because they do not

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.000
specifically mention the President.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.100
If Attorney General Barr imputed

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.820
those minority legal positions

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.480
onto Robert Mueller and the investigation,

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.820
then it was effectively
impossible, as a logical matter,

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:29.650
for the President to have
conducted obstruction of justice.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:31.300
Which brings me to point number eight:

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.160
Why did Barr quote the
portion of the Mueller Report

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.980
that states that the Mueller Report

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.140
does not exonerate the President?

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:41.380
The Barr Letter is potential
partisan whitewashing.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.180
We don't know what's in
the underlying report

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:45.190
and we don't know how
accurate of a summary

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:46.900
the Barr Letter actually is.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.620
It's possible that Barr is

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.510
intentionally setting the narrative

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:52.620
before the full Mueller Report comes out.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:56.590
But even still, why include
this cherry-picked phrase

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.070
that is actually detrimental
to the President,

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.850
stating that the Mueller Report does not,

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.910
in fact, exonerate the President?

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:04.360
If a report or evidence

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.660
doesn't exonerate someone from a crime

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.010
and you're writing a summary about it,

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:10.367
you don't have to include
a sentence that says,

00:11:10.367 --> 00:11:12.470
"The report does not
exonerate that person.".

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:14.900
You can just leave it at the fact that

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.060
the crime was not established

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.610
or that the decision was
made not to prosecute.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.490
You don't have to go to the extra step

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.460
and say that it doesn't
exonerate that person

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:24.910
and it seems like an odd inclusion

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:28.150
in this very high-level
summary of the Mueller Report.

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:29.410
Which takes me to point number nine,

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.310
which may be the most baffling
thing about the Barr Letter

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:35.190
and potentially, the
Mueller Report itself,

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.730
which is that there was a decision made

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:39.330
not to prosecute for
obstruction of justice,

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:40.820
but that decision was made

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.700
without interviewing the President.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.780
Was there an effort to actually
interview the President?

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:47.420
We know that under past precedent,

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:49.600
under the Clinton versus Jones affair

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.900
and also the Starr investigation
into President Clinton

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:57.040
that the President can be made
to stand for an interview.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.420
Was an effort to get President Trump

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.080
to stand for an interview made?

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.270
And on top of that,
why allow the President

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.440
to offer written answers
to written questions

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:08.580
in lieu of an actual oral examination?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:12.020
Obstruction of justice requires
proving that the defendant

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:15.445
had a corrupt motive
in conducting the acts

00:12:15.445 --> 00:12:17.780
that constitute the
obstruction of justice.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.260
The best way to determine that

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.350
is to interview the defendant.

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.000
Now, potentially, the defendant can

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:24.740
take the Fifth Amendment, but here,

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:27.920
given that the best evidence
one way or the other

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:31.050
is going to come from the
President about his motivations

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:33.340
in taking these different actions,

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:37.000
why was the President not
interviewed in this investigation?

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:38.710
Now that the investigation is done,

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:40.280
Attorney General Barr is going to have to

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.520
read through thousands of
pages of the Mueller Report

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:45.050
to determine what can
be publicly released.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.020
He could really benefit
from a speed reading class

